[38;5;252m[1m## The one real defect found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C is compiled without [38;5;10mNDEBUG[0m, so all ten [38;5;10massert()[0ms are live — the C [38;5;10m.so[0m imports [38;5;10m__assert_fail[0m. The Rust had them only as comments. That is observable: [38;5;10mstbds_hmdel_key[0m with [38;5;10mmode == 2[0m on a string map, deleting a non-final element, string-hashes the [3maddress[23m of the key field, gets [38;5;10mslot == -1[0m, and trips [38;5;10massert(slot >= 0)[0m at [38;5;10mlib.c:846[0m. The C aborted; the Rust silently did an out-of-bounds write at [38;5;10mstorage[-1][0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
All ten asserts are now implemented in [38;5;10mtranslation/src/lib.rs[0m, calling glibc [38;5;10m__assert_fail[0m with the same assertion text, line number, and function name. [38;5;10merr_25b_hmdel_mode2_middle_aborts[0m forks a child per library and confirms both die with [38;5;10mSignalled(6)[0m and identical messages; only the [38;5;10m__FILE__[0m prefix differs, since the C embeds its absolute build path.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Three other divergences turned out to be bugs in my tests, not the translation: uninitialized [38;5;10mrealloc[0m tail bytes and a dangling [38;5;10mtemp_key[0m (freed by the strdup delete path) — both UB to read in the C too, so they are excluded from snapshots with the reasoning documented inline.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two notes on [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m: row 3 was corrected after testing — [38;5;10marrgrowf(NULL, es, 0, 0)[0m returns [38;5;10mNULL[0m without allocating rather than bumping capacity to 4. Row 47 ([38;5;10marrfreef(NULL)[0m → [38;5;10mfree((void *) -32)[0m) is recorded but untested, as it is UB in the C itself and would abort the harness.[0m[0m
